    "result_text": "All tests pass: **264 run, 0 failures, 0 errors**, including the two new `AcceptanceTest` cases.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe locality derivation now prefers the postcode, falling back to the city table.\n\n**`OwnerLocality.java`** \u2014 added `forCityAndPostcode(city, postcode)`, which:\n1. Looks up the region by postcode range first (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099) via a new private `forPostcode` helper (validates a 4-digit code, then scans the ranges).\n2. Falls back to the existing `forCity` city-to-region table when the postcode is null, malformed, or outside all known ranges.\n\nThe original `forCity` is kept intact (it's still used by the controller's postcode validation).\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 the `locality` mapping expression now calls `forCityAndPostcode(owner.getCity(), owner.getPostcode())` instead of `forCity(owner.getCity())`.\n\nThis returns the same region for known cities (Sydney\u2192NSW, etc., since their pinned postcodes fall in the matching range) but disambiguates by postcode when a city is unknown or shares a name \u2014 e.g. an unknown city with postcode `3000` now yields `VIC`, as asserted by the new `functionalityPostcodePreferredOverCity` test.",
