    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, in-order list of everything applied when creating an owner via **POST /api/owners**. The endpoint is handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`).\n\n## Phase 0 \u2014 Security (before anything else)\n1. **`@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`** \u2014 caller must have `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN`, else **403**. (Enforcement depends on `petclinic.security.enable` / method security being on.)\n\n## Phase 1 \u2014 Bean Validation on the request body\nTriggered by `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` (declared on the generated `OwnersApi` interface). Any failure throws `MethodArgumentNotValidException`, handled by `ExceptionControllerAdvice` \u2192 **400** with field error details. Constraints on `OwnerFieldsDto`:\n2. **firstName** \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern(\"^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$\")`\n3. **lastName** \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern(\"^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$\")`\n4. **address** \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..255)`, `@Pattern(\".*\\S.*\")` (non-blank)\n5. **city** \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`, `@Pattern(\".*\\S.*\")`\n6. **telephone** \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n7. **email** \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`, `@Email` (optional)\n8. **postcode** \u2014 `@Pattern(\"^[0-9]{4}$\")` (optional)\n9. **registrationDate** \u2014 `@Valid` (optional)\n\n## Phase 2 \u2014 Controller body logic (in this exact order)\n10. **Map DTO \u2192 `Owner`** via `ownerMapper.toOwner`.\n11. **Address normalization** \u2014 trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand ST\u2192STREET / RD\u2192ROAD / AVE\u2192AVENUE. Empty result \u2192 **400**. *(mutates address)*\n12. **Telephone \u2192 E.164** (`toE164`) \u2014 strip separators; `+`kept, leading `0`\u2192`+61`, else `+1`; must be 8\u201315 digits and pass national-length check (`+61`=9, `+1`=10). Invalid \u2192 **400**. *(mutates telephone)*\n13. **Email normalization** (only if present) \u2014 trim, regex `^[^@\\s]+@[^@\\s]+\\.[^@\\s]+$`, lower-case. Invalid \u2192 **400**. *(mutates email)*\n14. **Postcode validation** (only if present) \u2014 must be `[0-9]{4}` and fall within the region range for its city (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099). Invalid \u2192 **400**.\n15. **Registration date defaulting** \u2014 if null, set to `LocalDate.now()`. *(mutates registrationDate)*\n16. **Business-day adjustment** (`toBusinessDay`) \u2014 roll Sat/Sun forward to Monday. *(mutates registrationDate)*\n17. **Per-city cap** \u2014 if `countOwnersInCity(city) >= 50` (`MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY`) \u2192 **409 CONFLICT**.\n18. **Per-day cap** \u2014 if `countOwnersRegisteredOn(date) >= 100` (`MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY`) \u2192 **429 TOO_MANY_REQUESTS**.\n19. **Household assignment** \u2014 find existing owners sharing normalized lastName+address, compute a deterministic `householdId` (SHA-256, first 12 hex, upper-cased), and **\u26a0\ufe0f side-effect: persist every existing household member whose `householdId` changed** via `clinicService.saveOwner(member)` \u2014 writes to *other* rows, each in its own transaction.\n20. **Duplicate/identity check** \u2014 build `identityKey = telephone|email|householdId`; if any existing owner matches \u2192 **409 CONFLICT**.\n21. **Set derived fields on the new owner**: `customerCode` (`CITY3-LAST3-NNNN`), `membershipNumber` (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`), `namesakeCount` (count of existing same first+last name).\n22. **Persist the new owner** \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` \u2192 `@Transactional`, `ownerRepository.save` (persist since id is null; `pets` cascade ALL).\n23. **Audit log side-effect** \u2014 one line to the dedicated `AUDIT` logger (`owner created: id=\u2026`).\n24. **Build response** \u2014 map to `OwnerDto`, set `bulkSignupWarning` flag (true if >80 owners registered today), set `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header \u2192 **201 CREATED**.\n\n## Notes\n- The **service layer is a thin pass-through** \u2014 all business logic/validation lives in the controller; `saveOwner` just delegates to the repository inside a transaction.\n- The **entity carries its own Bean Validation** (`Owner`/`Person`: `@NotEmpty` on firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone; telephone `@Pattern(\"^(\\+[0-9]{8,15}|[0-9]{10})$\")`), enforced by Hibernate on flush \u2014 a second validation layer behind the DTO.\n- **No JPA lifecycle callbacks / auditing** (`@PrePersist`, `@EntityListeners`, `@CreatedDate` etc.) exist \u2014 `registrationDate` is set manually, not by auditing.\n- **No email is sent and no Spring event is published** anywhere in this path; the only outbound \"notification\" is the AUDIT log line.\n- The controller itself is **not `@Transactional`**, so the household-member writes (step 19) and the new-owner save (step 22) commit as separate transactions."
